    "pubDate": "2024-04-15T18:14:20.987Z",
    "content": "In this tutorial, we’ll explore how to enhance an image viewer in React/NextJS by integrating zoom functionality. With this feature, users can zoom in on images for a closer look, improving the overall user experience. We’ll leverage React hooks to manage state and seamlessly integrate zoom capabilities into the existing image viewer component.\n\nUnderstanding the Setup\n\nBefore diving into the impl",
    "fullContent": "In this tutorial, we’ll explore how to enhance an image viewer in React/NextJS by integrating zoom functionality. With this feature, users can zoom in on images for a closer look, improving the overall user experience. We’ll leverage React hooks to manage state and seamlessly integrate zoom capabilities into the existing image viewer component.\n\nUnderstanding the Setup\n\nBefore diving into the implementation, let’s take a quick look at the code snippet I chose to illustrate how I get thngs working. The component, Carousel, (it doesn’t have to be a carousel, in this case it is) renders a collection of images and enables users to view them in a carousel layout. The goal is to extend this component to allow users to zoom in on individual images within the viewer.\n\nImplementing Zoom Functionality\n\nLet’s modify the existing Carousel component to incorporate zoom functionality:\n\nIn the modified Carousel component, clicking on an image triggers the openZoomedImage function, which sets the zoomedImage state to the URL of the clicked image. This renders the zoomed image overlay.\n\nStyling the Zoomed Image\n\nLet’s add some minimal styling to the zoomed image overlay:\n\nThis CSS ensures that the zoomed image is displayed centered on the screen with a semi-transparent overlay. Users can click anywhere on the zoomed image to close it and return to the viewer.\n\nThat’s it, an easy way to successfully add zoom functionality to your React/Next.JS image viewer component, enabling users to zoom in on images for a closer look. This enhancement improves the user experience and provides a more immersive way to interact with images within the viewer.\n\nGet Thomas Augot’s stories in your inbox\n\nJoin Medium for free to get updates from this writer.\n\nFeel free to customize the styling and functionality further to match your project’s requirements. Happy coding :)\n\nIf this article helped you, feel free to connect with me!",
