    "content": "A Time-Saving Blueprint for Faster Website Development\n\nAre you tired of spending hours setting up the basic structure for your Next.js projects? Look no further! I’ve just released a GitHub repository containing a comprehensive boilerplate code for a Next.js app with Tailwind CSS, designed to turbocharge your development process.\n\nWhy Use This Boilerplate?\n\nAs a full-stack web developer, I unders",
    "fullContent": "A Time-Saving Blueprint for Faster Website Development\n\nAre you tired of spending hours setting up the basic structure for your Next.js projects? Look no further! I’ve just released a GitHub repository containing a comprehensive boilerplate code for a Next.js app with Tailwind CSS, designed to turbocharge your development process.\n\nWhy Use This Boilerplate?\n\nAs a full-stack web developer, I understand the importance of efficiency, especially when starting a new project. That’s why I created this Next.js and Tailwind CSS boilerplate — a ready-to-use foundation that can save you an entire day of coding.\n\nThat’s how the app look after you ran it on your local server:\n\nWho Can Benefit?\n\nThis boilerplate is perfect for freelancers and developers looking to kickstart their projects faster. Imagine starting your next website project with a fully functional Navbar, a basic homepage, and contact page — all in a matter of minutes.\n\nHow to Get Started?\n\nDon’t let repetitive setup tasks slow you down. Use this Next.js and Tailwind CSS boilerplate to accelerate your project setup and get to coding the interesting stuff faster. Whether you’re a freelancer or a developer on a tight schedule, this time-saving tool is designed to make your life easier.\n\nGet Thomas Augot’s stories in your inbox\n\nJoin Medium for free to get updates from this writer.\n\nReady to get started? Check out the repository here, follow the documentation of the repo to get started and supercharge your Next.js projects today!\n\nFind me on GitHub: https://github.com/thomasaugot\nConnect with me on LinkedIn",
