    "content": "Today, let’s delve into the fascinating realm of implementing dark mode in a React app using SCSS. By the end of this guide, your app will have a sleek appearance that adapts seamlessly to different lighting conditions.\n\nSetting the Stage\n\nFirstly, let’s set up a Dark Mode context using React’s Context API. To proceed, I chose to add a new folder to the /src folder of my project called “context”, ",
    "fullContent": "Today, let’s delve into the fascinating realm of implementing dark mode in a React app using SCSS. By the end of this guide, your app will have a sleek appearance that adapts seamlessly to different lighting conditions.\n\nSetting the Stage\n\nFirstly, let’s set up a Dark Mode context using React’s Context API. To proceed, I chose to add a new folder to the /src folder of my project called “context”, in which I created a DarkModeContext.js file. Here’s a brief overview, you can simply just copy/paste this code:\n\nNow, let’s demystify the SCSS setup. In my /styles folder, I created a variables.scss file, in which I have added the following code:\n\nNow, let’s elevate our app’s style!\n\nStep 1: Context-Driven Dark Mode\n\nOur Dark Mode is controlled by the Context API. To toggle between light and dark, we call setMode. Here's how you can integrate this into your component:\n\nStep 2: SCSS Wizardry\n\nNow, let’s demystify the SCSS magic. The variables.scss file holds the key. Each mode in $modes represents a set of color variables. The @mixin mode dynamically applies these colors based on the chosen mode.\n\nGet Thomas Augot’s stories in your inbox\n\nJoin Medium for free to get updates from this writer.\n\nFor the styles you haven’t already defined in the variable.scss file, you can do it directly from the component’s own scss file. To proceed, in your yourComponent.scss, apply the selected mode's styles to your components:\n\nAnd there you have it! With the Context API steering our dark mode ship and SCSS coloring our styles, your app is ready to adapt gracefully, day or night.\n\nDark mode isn’t just a trend; it’s a practical feature that enhances user experience. By combining React’s Context API with the flexibility of SCSS, we’ve now equipped our app with a seamless and stylish dark mode experience.\n\nHappy coding! 🌑",
